(2. PostgreSQL 19 Released) Tj
T*
(Source: Simon Willison's Weblog | Published: 2026-11-19T20:43:57+00:00) Tj
T*
(Link: https://simonwillison.net/2026/Nov/19/postgresql-19/) Tj
T*
(PostgreSQL 19 Released Most years PostgreSQL ships a new release in September, but this year's) Tj
T*
(release came two months later thanks mainly to the flurry of issues that the PostgreSQL team) Tj
T*
(needed to address as part of the ongoing AI-reported vulnerability apocalypse. This release was) Tj
T*
(definitely worth the wait. My favorite new feature is this one: For applications that send) Tj
T*
(reads to standbys, PostgreSQL 19 adds "read-your-writes" consistency with the new WAIT FOR LSN) Tj
T*
(command. A session on a standby can use WAIT FOR LSN to wait until the standby has replayed the) Tj
T*
(write-ahead log \(WAL\) up to a specific log sequence number \(LSN\) before running a query, so the) Tj
T*
(application can read data it just wrote on the primary. In practice, that looks like this:) Tj
T*
(UPDATE movie SET genre = 'Dramatic' WHERE genre = 'Drama'; SELECT pg_current_wal_insert_lsn\(\);) Tj
T*
(That returns a value like 0/0306EE20 . Store that somewhere \(a signed cookie would work\) such) Tj
T*
(that on a subsequent request your application can do: WAIT FOR LSN '0/0306EE20' WITH \(TIMEOUT) Tj
T*
('0.1s'\); SELECT * FROM movie WHERE genre = 'Drama'; The timeout is optional - if you provide) Tj
T*
(one you'll get an error if the replica you are talking to doesn't catc...) Tj
T*
